    "body": "DUNCAN_NIGHT_REPORT_R01\nCYCLE_ID = DNR01-20260830-009\nSOURCE_WINDOW = 2026-08-30 / fresh cycle after accepted DNR01-20260830-008 and current main b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1\nMAIN_HEAD_OBSERVED = b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1\nDAY_EVENTS_REVIEWED = issue #204 restore entrypoint; issue #206 Night School contract and cycle 008 postverify; issue #199 character drawing law; PR #111 cycle 008 accepted report; Permanent Archive V1 current protected archive path\nANIME_TOPICS_STUDIED = animation timing / spacing / impact readability / hold-acceleration-impact-settle rhythm\nOPEN_SOURCE_CODE_INSPECTED = OpenToonz opentoonz/opentoonz master exact ref a0272090f7a5c210702cf55567a2691556275cb5 / BSD-3-Clause for OpenToonz core / repository pushed 2026-08-30T01:54:56Z / toonz/sources/common/tparam/tdoublekeyframe.cpp / TDoubleKeyframe supports Constant Linear Exponential SpeedInOut EaseInOut EaseInOutPercentage and step exposure; integration cost for ZORR timing study = LOW because existing keyframe/interpolation concepts can be reused without new animation framework\nREFERENCE_PRINCIPLES = extract timing principle only: readable impact comes from unequal spacing and controlled holds, not from copying any copyrighted shot; OpenToonz demonstrates mature explicit interpolation/exposure primitives instead of requiring a custom timing engine\nEXERCISES = normalized 0-to-1 move compared across Linear, symmetric smoothstep, and bounded hold-to-accelerate-to-impact-to-settle profiles; base test used 12 sampled frames; changed/unseen test used 18 frames and different physical travel scale; metrics = peak interval displacement / mean interval displacement, hold fraction, largest-three-interval travel share, monotonicity, endpoint\nVERIFICATION = base 12-frame linear impact-concentration=1.000 top3-share=0.2727 hold-frac=0.000; smoothstep impact-concentration=1.4959 top3-share=0.3989; impact-profile impact-concentration=2.6649 top3-share=0.6661 hold-frac=0.3636 monotonic=YES endpoint=1.000; changed 18-frame impact-profile impact-concentration=2.9740 top3-share=0.4587 hold-frac=0.4118 monotonic=YES endpoint=1.000\nFAILURES = none in bounded arithmetic exercise; universal perceptual threshold is NOT PROVEN; real Tier-1 character-motion transfer is NOT PROVEN\nROOT_CAUSES = sampling density changes numeric impact-concentration, so one fixed threshold cannot be promoted from synthetic timing alone; perceptual timing also depends on pose design, smear/shape change, camera and sound that were outside this bounded test\nREGRESSION_RESULTS = cycle-008 chroma-hierarchy principle replayed fresh with OpenCV 4.13.0 Lab conversion: restrained palette focal chroma lead=71.8995; adding a competing saturated blue reduced unique lead to 8.3293, preserving prior conclusion that accent strength is relational rather than saturation alone\nTRANSFER_TEST = unseen 18-frame / different travel-scale timing profile preserved the qualitative hierarchy versus linear and smoothstep while remaining monotonic and landing exactly at endpoint; quantitative metric shifted with sampling, therefore skill remains PARTIAL\nSKILL_DELTA =\n- impact_spacing_qc: UNTESTED -> PARTIAL\nSELF_MODEL_DELTA =\n- TIMING_RELATION_RULE = judge impact by spacing relationships and holds before adding drawings or effects\n- TIMING_SCALE_RULE = normalize motion before comparing different travel distances or shot scales\n- TIMING_CONFIDENCE_RULE = do not promote a synthetic frame-spacing ratio into a universal perceptual threshold without real character-motion transfer\nOWNER_TASTE_SIGNALS = issue #199 confirms controlled hierarchy and macro-before-micro discipline; current exercise applies the same restraint principle temporally without asserting a new OWNER animation law\nOWNER_TASTE_MODEL_DELTA =\n- CONTROLLED_TEMPORAL_HIERARCHY = supporting inference only from existing restraint and hierarchy laws; not an OWNER lock and not a fixed timing ratio\nZORR_APPLICATION = use mature keyframe/interpolation/exposure primitives such as OpenToonz-style Constant/Linear/SpeedInOut/EaseInOut/step concepts for blocking and timing experiments; evaluate normalized spacing concentration before spending drawings/VFX; preserve existing locked ZORR timing whenever one exists\nPRIME_CORE_CHANGED = NO\nPRODUCTION_MUTATION = NO\nNEXT_TARGETS = real non-mutating Tier-1 motion transfer when durable frames/trajectory evidence is available; compare pose readability plus spacing; inspect OpenToonz xsheet/exposure code and OpenTimelineIO timing representation before any custom timeline logic",
